Syntax: mindthrust <victim>

Mind thrust is a focused offensive power that drives a sharp mental spike
into an enemy's consciousness. Unlike the broad disruption of a psionic
blast, mind thrust is precise and penetrating, designed to cause intense
pain and interrupt concentration.

The attack manifests as a sudden, stabbing pain in the victim's mind.
Beyond the immediate damage, the thrust can severely disrupt spellcasters
attempting to complete complex magical workings. Multiple independent
distraction effects may trigger, potentially ruining their spell.

This makes mind thrust particularly effective against enemy mages or
clerics who rely on tasked spells. A well-timed thrust can interrupt
their casting entirely, forcing them to begin again.

The power initiates combat if the psionicist is not already engaged with
the target. If used in combat, it can be directed at the current opponent
without specifying a target.

Mind thrust requires moderate skill to develop and consumes a reasonable
amount of mana for each use. It cannot be used while focusing your mind,
as the concentration required for mind focus precludes offensive
projection.

See Also: PSIONICS, PSIONIC BLAST, PSYCHIC CRUSH, MIND FOCUS

